summary:
- University: City University of Hong Kong
- Department: Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences
- Project: A One-health Investigation into the Zoonotic Potential of Malassezia Yeasts from the Skin of Man's Best Friends, Canis Familiaris and Felis Catus
- Duties:
- Benchtop laboratory: fungal agar production, culture analysis, DNA/RNA extraction, cPCR/qPCR, susceptibility testing via microdilution;
- Data analysis: assist in data sequencing, phylogenetic analysis, and statistical analysis;
- Sample curation: coordinate and maintain clinical sample banks, including sample processing and high-fidelity data entry;
- Field work: provide support for field works;
- Documentation and reporting: document and present findings and assist in preparing reports and publications;
- Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor.
- Requirements:
- A Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Science or related disciplines.
- Excellent communication skills and a strong work ethic;
- ability to work independently and collaboratively;
- willingness and ability to respond to challenges and to acquire new skills are required.
- Salary: and Conditions of Service offered will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Fringe benefits include leave, medical and dental consultations at the campus clinic.
- Contact: hrojob@cityu.edu.hk; 2788 1154; 3442 0311; 2026-2027
